    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "In an experiment to determine the Young modulus $E$ of the material of a wire, the measurements taken are shown."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "mass hung on end of wire $m = 2.300 \\pm 0.002\\,\\text{kg}$"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "original length of wire $l = 2.864 \\pm 0.005\\,\\text{m}$"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "diameter of wire $d = 0.82 \\pm 0.01\\,\\text{mm}$"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "extension of wire $e = 7.6 \\pm 0.2\\,\\text{mm}$"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "The Young modulus is calculated using"
    },
    {
      "type": "equation",
      "latex": "E = \\dfrac{4mgl}{\\pi d^{2} e}"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "where $g$ is the acceleration of free fall."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "The calculated value of $E$ is $1.61 \\times 10^{10}\\,\\text{N m}^{-2}$."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "How should the calculated value of $E$ and its uncertainty be expressed?"
    }
  ],
